{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Your arrows</b> — At first he mentioned \"your sword,\" and he also says \"your arrows,\" for they are sharp when the peoples are beneath you." "<b>They shall pierce</b> — Your arrows shall pierce the heart of — your enemies; therefore the word יפלו comes in the place of an etnaḥ, as though it were in construct state, for it serves on account of two words."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:52.549698459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}